      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, I can provide you with some general guidelines to help you make safe choices. When you're looking for high-protein foods suitable for MAOI users, it's best to focus on fresh, unprocessed options and be careful with meats, as well as fermented, smoked, or aged cheeses. Safe meats might include chicken, turkey, eggs, and fresh fish. As for cheeses, stick to young, fresh cheeses like Ricotta, cottage cheese, or Mozzarella. For protein sources, consider non-meat options like legumes (beans, lentils, and chickpeas), tofu, and quinoa. Always check the labels for any additional sources of tyramine or potential allergens. Stick to fresh or frozen produce that isn't been aged, cured, or fermented to minimize risk. Remember, although these suggestions can help you maintain a high-protein diet, the best course of action remains to consult with your doctor as soon as possible to discuss your specific situation and get detailed, personalized advice.",
